From 2801d2792ea6f16706c310a4cfb1554c4084bcf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:20:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] feat: let separately compiled mods provide message
 services

MessageService is internal, so a mod assembly cannot derive from it.
Mods now derive from the public ModMessageService (a plain object with
[MessageHandler] methods, SendToSocket and GetSocketAccount) and
register the type in the existing game/login message service
registries. When at least one is registered, the service factory adds
one internal ModMessageServiceHost per session: a real MessageService
child of the SessionActor whose MessageHandlers include the mod
services' message types, so the session's own dispatch table routes
those messages to it. The host creates the mod services and calls their
handlers on its actor thread; a constructor or handler exception is
logged against the mod and does not stop the session.

ReceiveProtocolDispatcher.MessageHandlers gets a protected setter so the
host can publish the merged table. Without mod services the factories
return their built-in sets unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: [AI session link removed]
